<details><summary>Reveal the controlled-composition definition</summary>
A controlled composition consists of an equivalence relation, a compatible binary operation, a weak unit, an associator between the two triple composites, and left and right unitors. When parallel transformations are unique, the pentagon and all other parallel coherence diagrams commute automatically.
</details>

## From parentheses to geometry

The five ways to parenthesize four atoms form a pentagon. Its edges are elementary reassociations, and its two routes between extreme vertices describe parallel coherence transformations. See the [associahedron overview](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Associahedron) for broader geometric context.

{{visualization:1}}

{{algorithm:0}}

<details><summary>Reveal the Reassociation Soundness Theorem</summary>
Every chain generated by associator moves, inverses, transitivity, and moves inside either argument evaluates to a coherent equivalence. The proof follows the chain recursively and uses compatibility of composition for contextual moves.
</details>

## Strict fingerprints before quotienting

Bounded continuation traces retain exact word information. Experiment with a prefix and observe every extension that remains inside the selected radius.

